Ticket #4471 is marked known, but it combines two causes. Split the reports by tenant locale and booking-form behavior, not by subject or intake tag.

<ReportSplit ticket={4471} />

## Shared parser: day and month reversed

The shared parser reads month first. For tenants whose locale writes the day first, dates can flip. This is the larger group: app, email, and booking-v2 form reports across the day-first tenant directory.

Filed as [openbeck/mega#1](https://github.com/openbeck/mega/issues/1) · 379 reports.

## Booking-v3 hint: displayed order disagrees with tenant parsing

Booking-v3 displays `MM/DD/YYYY`. In the three affected day-first tenants, people follow that hint while the form interprets the date using the tenant's locale. Keep this as a separate issue from the shared parser: the form's displayed instruction is the cause.

Filed as [openbeck/mega#2](https://github.com/openbeck/mega/issues/2) · 33 reports.

## Counting rule

The export contains overlapping rows. Count each report ID once, as the KB's `uniqueById` helper does. The figures above describe the export snapshot from 2026-10-04; the support desk may receive more reports after that date. Intake's `parser` and `hint` tags are guesses, so use the tenant locale, channel, and form version to classify a report.

